WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.650
The second match of the semifinals of
the Pantasia newcomers’ battle has begun.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.650
The opponent is the man claimed to be the
strongest of the newcomers, Suwabara Kai.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.900
I’m sorry, Suwabara.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.110
I’m winning this match.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.060
This is, without a doubt, the Earth’s best croissant,

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.120
Super Vapor-Action Croissant,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.120
Six Hundred Forty-Eight!

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.250
Croissant

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.590
Dave has... Dave has...

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.840
Dave has stood, and then died!

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.760
It’s no use, Kuroyanagi-san’s the same.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.260
Th... This is...

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.330
Could this be heaven?

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.270
Heaven really does exist!

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.920
Would you like to stop by first?

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.780
It’s the stop-by heaven for those
who’ve been here for 15 minutes.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.680
You look like her,

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.240
like Cathy.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.500
I like you, too, Kuroyanagi-san...

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:58.740
Satsuki...

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.690
But... it’s impossible.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.780
Because, you’re not dead yet.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.790
What?!

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.940
Kuroyanagi-san,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.590
please live well.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.180
They didn’t pay.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.980
M-M-M-M... Mei-Mei-Mei-Mei-Mei...

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:24.520
Yo.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.520
Azuma!

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.960
You’re the victor!

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.520
You’ve really made a bread delicious enough to die for!

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.700
With the <i>Japan</i> #44 made with petalite,

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.280
Kazuma crushed Suwabara.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.870
And all who have advanced to the finals are now gathered.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.310
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.230
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:53.530
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.030
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:02.120
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.790
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:23.130
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:31.100
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:38.970
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:46.690
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:54.160
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:03.540
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:12.300
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:16.560
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.550
is the light of only you.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:23.300
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:28.110
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:35.830
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.510
Just before the finals!!

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.970
The black shadow that approaches Kazuma!

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:56.100
Azuma-san.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.070
We’ve finally made it here.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.760
At the preliminaries and the first round of the finals...

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.520
and then again at the second round and the third round,

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:09.700
you produced results that greatly
exceeded our expectations and won.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.980
T-This is...

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.150
Vapor action!

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.980
Ac-choon! Ac-choon! Ac-choon! Ac-choon!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.610
Annoying!

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.990
Not paper, but vapor!

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.450
All right, then.
One melon bread coming up...

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:31.960
W-What the?

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.210
Azuma-san, what are you...?

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.300
All right, sorry for the wait!
One melon bread, all done.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:43.810
Let’s go.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.760
O-Oh no!

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.970
I guess it came, after all!

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.700
MELON!!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.000
Victor: Azuma Kazuma!

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.330
All right!

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.830
Once more!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.590
All right!

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.620
Bring that okonomiyaki sandwich to my mouth!

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.380
Azuma!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.260
All right! Here!

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.480
Chomp.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.640
This thing!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.600
The French rolls of the given theme
have been crushed like an okonomiyaki,

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.860
and a sauce-soaked
yakisoba has been added in between.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:39.860
In other words,

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.230
an Onono Komachi-san...!

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:43.440
I mean, an okonomiyaki sandwich!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.610
Victor: Azuma Kazuma!

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.950
No way!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.740
All right!

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.680
He’s spinning like crazy!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.020
But, what’s this?!

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.730
Can’t you see it?!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.310
Right now, he’s truly become...

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.660
the monster from outer space...

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.160
Victor: Azuma Kazuma!

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.370
And, finally...

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:38.960
And with this,

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.880
the 39th Pantasia newcomers’ battle finalists are...

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.630
Azuma Kazuma from the A block.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.130
And Kanmuri Shigeru from the B block.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.470
The victor will get a prize of 1,000,000 yen,

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.020
an extra prize of studying abroad in France,

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:58.020
and a special chance to work at the Main Branch.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.650
The theme, of course, is whatever you like.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.070
We look forward to a
wonderful match as befitting the finals.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.360
But, the opponent this time is
different from our earlier opponents.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:11.870
Kanmuri Shigeru is...

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.830
the partner of my stepsister, Yukino.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.790
We must not let our guards down, Azuma-san...

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.000
We must coordinate with
everyone at work for the next match.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.040
The day of the finals, one week from now,

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.300
is expected to bring in many
more spectators than the semifinals.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.470
In order to avoid chaos,

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.720
Note: SP likely stands for “Service Personnel”.
the SP’s will usher regular people in at the main gate.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.550
People from the press will enter from the west gate.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:38.940
And I request that Pantasia
people come in from the east gate.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.310
Azuma-kun.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.310
Congratulations on advancing to the finals.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.320
The masked geezer.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:49.410
But, to think that it was
bread delicious enough to die for...

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:54.200
For having suspected you...

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.280
please forgive me.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.450
That’s fine.
Don’t worry about it.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.000
Even with <i>Japan</i> #44,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.830
unless it’s been made really well,

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.750
you don’t go to heaven.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.670
Since it was so sudden, you
must have been surprised, right?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:09.840
Yes, it really surprised me.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:10.680
In various ways.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:14.260
Oh, come to think of it, Grandpa Umasaburou in Gifu...

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.510
I wonder if he wasn’t sleeping, but had
instead gone to heaven at that time...

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.610
I really want to go again...

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.440
Oh well. Whatever.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.440
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.450
Don’t worry about it, Meister-han.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:35.910
Kawachi.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.160
I’m a friend and even I suspected him a little...

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.290
It’s not surprising that you suspected him.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:44.580
Me, too. For a moment I wondered what would happen...

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.790
Thank you very much.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.800
By the way, Kawachi-san.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:54.300
The results of the investigation are in,
and we know why your dough did not rise.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.390
Protein hydrolyzing enzymes.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.300
Endoproteases.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.350
Endou catches a cold in the bath?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:07.730
A minuscule amount of hydrolytic enzymes
like proteases are present naturally in flour.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.480
But, according to the investigation’s report,

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.780
Kawachi-san, in your dough,

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.530
more than 10,000 times the
usual amount was detected.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:18.990
It must be Yukino.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.830
The SP who brought in the ingredients is missing.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.750
We have no proof.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.750
We will continue the inquiry, but...

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.250
any specifics as to who is to blame are...

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.130
But...!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.260
It’s all right.
But...!

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:33.510
It’s all right. It’s all right.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.170
Kawachi...

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.640
Even if we were to have a rematch due
to an irregularity having been discovered,

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.930
I don’t think I can win against Kanmuri.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.050
But...

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.810
Really, it’s all right now.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.690
I’ll have my revenge...

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.730
when he wins.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.110
Azuma promised me this... right?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.440
I leave it to you, Azuma!

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.450
Kawachi...

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.030
All right.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.990
I’m a little tired.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.000
I’ll just watch the match at leisure.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:08.500
At leisure?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.580
What are you going to do about the third place match?

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:12.250
What?

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.260
The third place match will occur on
the afternoon of the day of the finals.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.380
I believe that the announcement
should be any time now.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.510
What?

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:23.390
I will now announce the
participants of the third place match.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:26.140
From the Main Branch, Suwabara Kai.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:29.070
From the Southern Tokyo Branch, Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.190
The third place match.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.110
I get to... do it with Suwabara!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.410
While it’s between two people who’ve lost...

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:41.120
it’s you who will conclude the newcomers’ battle.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:45.000
Using today’s defeat to induce you
to greater heights in breadmaking.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.160
That’s all.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.250
Third place...

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.080
Should you be the third place winner,

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.210
along with a prize of 300,000
yen and studying abroad in France,

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.380
you may apply for employment at the Main Branch.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.390
Th-th-th-th... The Main Branch?!

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.180
Wait a minute.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.440
In that case, only the amount of the
prize money differs from the championship!

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.440
This year, the number of people was large.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.360
So, we decided to give extra
incentives to the third place winner as well.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.940
In my time, the third place
winner only had the prize money.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.290
Pantasia has also become rather magnanimous.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.410
There was no prize money in my time.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.910
It was the Pantasia special backpack.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:26.830
A backpack...

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.910
Just a backpack...

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:31.380
And, by the way,
fourth place winner will...

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.000
get a collector’s card worth 2000 yen.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.000
Wow.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:40.630
That’s quite a difference in the
treatment of third and fourth place winners.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:43.350
I can’t lose this one at any cost.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:43.890
Kawachi!

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.730
I’m beginning to really get back into this.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.060
Kawachi!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.100
Is what I’d like to say, but...

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.350
my opponent is that Suwabara.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:53.900
I...

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.940
I don’t know if I can win.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.320
Kawachi!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.360
When exactly did I get on his shoulders?

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.120
Or rather... What are you doing, Manager?

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.410
You have one week.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:07.330
Go over here.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.800
A church?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:12.710
Over there...

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:17.750
Ah! That’s the place that led to
you getting that hair style, right?

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.140
It’s not that kind of place.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.470
It’s the place where I learned

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.510
the most important thing
about bread from a certain person.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:31.730
You’ve become strong.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:35.810
But, when you come up against geniuses
like Kanmuri or Suwabara as opponents,

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.270
it’s a fact that you tend to beat yourself up.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.360
Yeah...

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.740
That’s true.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:44.780
I hate it, but it’s true.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.990
So, go forth!

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.280
And win!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.030
All right!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.000
Work hard, Kawachi!

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.380
Hey!

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:56.500
It’s not just me.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.800
You have to work just as hard.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.050
When I come back for the third place match,

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.510
I won’t forgive you if you’ve lost.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.720
He won’t forgive me!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.980
Everyone at the Southern
Tokyo Branch really gets along well.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.650
You can really make that out?

00:13:15.650 --> 00:13:18.160
Or rather, what the hell am I doing?

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:24.040
Well, I’m off.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:28.410
Oh, that’s right.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.490
Azuma, there was something I had to tell you.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:36.830
I noticed during my match with Kanmuri.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.580
If appears that his weapon is
not limited to the Kaiyou yeast.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.840
Like you, Kanmuri may have Solar Hands.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.390
Kanmuri has...

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.240
Like you, Kanmuri may have Solar Hands.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.620
Kanmuri has...

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.330
Is that true?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.420
I can’t be sure.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:23.340
But... the feel of that
fermentation was the same as Azuma’s.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.590
No, at least,

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.340
there’s no mistaking that it’s at about the same level.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.840
Kanmuri has...

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:35.390
But, it’s also a fact that in
addition to the Solar Gauntlets,

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:38.940
there are other ways to warm
your hands as Suwabara did.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.400
Kanmuri is a scientist.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:47.940
It’s possible that he warms
his hands using some technique.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.770
But it’s fine.

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:51.200
What?

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:52.700
It doesn’t matter.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:53.950
Azuma-san.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.410
I have the Solar Hands as well.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.460
So, we’re even.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.420
That’s true, but...

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.970
Kanmuri-san also has the Kaiyou yeast.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:07.840
Don’t worry.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:10.640
If Kanmuri has the Kaiyou yeast,

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.470
I have the petalite board.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:14.600
Like I’d lose!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:15.770
But...

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:17.850
Even with that, the conditions are even.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.350
There’s no guarantee anywhere that we’ll win.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.520
It’s all right.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:23.060
Azuma-san...

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.110
Yeah, it’s just as Azuma says.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.240
You’re such a worry-wart.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.410
Kawachi-san!

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.520
Relax, Tsukino.

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.030
It’s not even.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:35.410
You haven’t forgotten, right?

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.500
Azuma has something important that Kanmuri doesn’t.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.540
At the Southern Tokyo Branch,

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.420
we have trust amongst each
other that won’t lose to anyone and...

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:48.920
We have each other.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.260
So, just relax, Tsukino.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.600
For your sake, and for Kawachi’s sake,

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.020
I’ll definitely win. So, don’t worry.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:58.220
Okay.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.730
Come to think of it,

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.230
I left the board at the hall.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.190
I’m going to get it!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.240
Some things never change.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.860
But, it looks like there’s no need to worry.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:14.960
I’m off then.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.330
Take care, Kawachi-san!

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.830
Everybody, thank you very much.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:33.980
There were so many people, yet
after everyone leaves, it’s quiet, isn’t it?

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.760
Don’t avoid the subject.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:39.510
What was it you wanted to talk about?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.110
I have a request.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:47.020
Money?

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.480
Can I have you promise that
you won’t interfere with the finals?

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.700
Boy...!

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.120
Do you know who it is you’re talking to?

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:01.580
Yes!

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.120
Who else do you think is here?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:05.920
I think I’ve told you already!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.800
It’s not enough to just win against those cockroaches.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.500
I’m going to have them shamed and crushed.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.640
But, it’s the finals next.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.430
Because of the thing with Kawachi-san’s
dough, there’s an investigation in progress.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:23.690
And I think that General Manager Kirisaki
will have even stronger security in place.

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:26.850
I think that any scheming beyond this would be suicidal.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.900
Kirisaki...

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.980
Yeah, he’s a bit of a pain.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.450
As soon as I become the true successor of Pantasia,

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.990
I’ll tear off that mask of his
and drive him out.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.250
So, since you’re saying so much,

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:44.370
you’re sure you’ll win, right, boy?

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.500
You’re facing a bread that sends you to heaven.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.170
The existence of something
like heaven is dubious in real life.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:54.010
So, there’s no way you
could possibly go there, is there?

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:59.010
That hyper-sensitive senpai of ours
probably just happened to feel that way

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:01.520
and was caught up in some sort of illusion.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:05.020
Something like that is no problem
if I get serious.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:07.890
How very promising.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:12.690
But, a low down dirty sow like you,

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.400
interested in nothing but money,

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:18.030
would only go to hell.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:21.450
Whatever. I promise.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:22.830
Thank you very much.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.880
But, don’t forget...

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:33.510
Who exactly is paying the high research
costs for your cute little germs

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:37.550
and the maintenance costs for the
facilities to make your bread.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.300
It’s Yukino-sama!

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.210
Sow!

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.770
Well, I’ll be off then.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.990
There’s research I need to do to win.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:00.460
I don’t like fighting for that woman, but...

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.830
I’m looking forward to it, Azuma-kun.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:04.840
With you,

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.330
it seems I can fight it out in a fair
and square, serious match.

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:11.790
With my new Kaiyou yeast currently being researched...

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.180
With RAS...

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.300
and these Solar Hands...

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.800
Kanmuri has a point.

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.730
It’s dangerous to do anything in the finals.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.430
But...

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.900
Just winning is boring...

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:32.560
Like with the blondie,

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:35.020
if I don’t have them crumble...

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.740
Just remembering it makes me laugh.

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:48.290
Oh?

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.250
What’s this board?

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.020
Umm, St. Andrew’s Church.

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:09.770
Andrew’s Church...

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.730
It’s just ahead after I turn at that corner, right?

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.320
St. Andrew’s Church

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.900
The... The ivy has...

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.000
wound itself all over and...

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.620
it looks like...

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.580
an a-a-afro.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.590
I-I have a bad feeling...

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.050
Azuma-san is late, isn’t he?

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.560
It’s been almost an hour.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:50.560
Azuma!

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.180
Azuma-san...

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.440
Oh, where’s the board?

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:57.520
It’s disappeared.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.110
What?

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:01.320
It’s disappeared.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.610
I left it in the oven, but...

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.710
There was no one in the hall.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:10.120
I asked a custodian who was nearby, but...

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:16.290
all he saw was a tall woman leave the hall last...

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:17.120
What?

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.130
A tall woman?

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:30.760
Hey kids...

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.350
Playing in the sand looks fun.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:38.360
Can Big Sis play, too?

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:40.530
What?

00:21:40.530 --> 00:21:41.860
What do you want to do?

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.450
I’ll give you something nice, so let me join you.

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:44.870
Here.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.360
Pretty sand.

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:49.570
It’s shining.

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:57.580
Oh, there’s some stones mixed in as well.

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:00.380
What kind of sand is this?

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.630
Who knows...

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:05.090
I’m not too sure myself.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:12.600
He called it petalite or something.

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:16.100
Weird name.

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.820 --> 00:24:08.130
The final match of the Pantasia Newcomers' Battle is beginning!

00:24:08.130 --> 00:24:09.840
We're finally at the finals!

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:12.090
But is Azuma going to be all ri–

00:24:12.090 --> 00:24:14.590
Look out! Jab it! Jab it some more!

00:24:14.590 --> 00:24:16.060
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:18.910
The Sticky Showdown!!
Azuma Kazuma VS Kanmuri Shigeru!

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:23.600
We have the proverb series relating to bread, #1.

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:24.230
Relating to bread

00:24:24.230 --> 00:24:25.770
The proverb series #1

00:24:25.770 --> 00:24:25.820
We have the proverb series relating to bread, #1.

00:24:25.820 --> 00:24:25.900
Bread is better than the song of birds.

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:27.030
Bread is better than the song of birds
Bread is better than the song of birds.

00:24:27.030 --> 00:24:28.870
This is an old proverb in the West.

00:24:28.870 --> 00:24:28.950
Dumplings are better than flowers
This is an old proverb in the West.

00:24:28.950 --> 00:24:31.740
It has the same meaning as the Japanese proverb, “Dumplings are better than flowers.”

00:24:31.990 --> 00:24:34.120
Really?
